    prompt: "[Reading 34 lines from start (total: 34 lines, 0 remaining)]\r\n\r\n# Asymmetrical Bob\r\n\r\nCreate a true asymmetrical bob defined by a deliberate, immediately visible difference in side length.\r\n\r\n## ASYMMETRY GEOMETRY\r\n\r\n- One side must terminate visibly higher, around the jaw to upper-neck region.\r\n- The opposite side must remain visibly longer, extending toward the lower jaw, upper neck, or shoulder direction according to the source framing.\r\n- The length difference must be built into the haircut perimeter itself, not created by sweeping symmetrical hair across the face.\r\n- The perimeter should travel continuously through the back and side sections while preserving the intentional left/right imbalance.\r\n- The asymmetry must remain obvious from the source viewing angle without becoming exaggerated or theatrical.\r\n\r\n## SILHOUETTE\r\n\r\n- Maintain a controlled bob silhouette with a clean, intentional lower perimeter.\r\n- The shorter side and longer side must read as parts of one coherent haircut, not disconnected sections.\r\n- Do not turn the design into a generic angled lob, pixie-bob, or ordinary symmetrical bob.\r\n- Keep face framing subordinate to the primary asymmetrical perimeter.\r\n- Do not introduce bangs unless bangs already exist in the source hairstyle.\r\n\r\n## TEXTURE AND WEIGHT\r\n\r\n- Maintain controlled natural volume with enough lower weight to preserve the bob identity.\r\n- Use realistic strand grouping and subtle independent fibre variation around the perimeter.\r\n- The cut edge should be professionally controlled but never ruler-straight or CGI-perfect.\r\n- Roots must emerge naturally from the existing scalp with believable density and directional flow.\r\n\r\n## STYLE RECOGNITION\r\n\r\nThe result must immediately read as a premium asymmetrical bob. The defining visual signal is the deliberate shorter-side/longer-side relationship, not a side-swept styling effect.\r\n\r\n## NEGATIVE CONSTRAINTS\r\n\r\nNo symmetrical bob, ordinary angled bob, generic lob, pixie-bob, fake side-sweep used to simulate asymmetry, or new bangs. Do not alter the face, jaw, chin, neck, ears, skin, lighting, background, framing, perspective, or source hair colour.",
